{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Notice was given before the point of deviation and the rider agreed to it: MSG-05006-003 (driver, sent 18:01:46) asked 'Miss, AYE jam already, I go West Coast Highway can?', the rider read it at 18:02:06 and answered 'ok' at 18:02:11 (MSG-05006-004, read 18:02:35), and the platform's own event record puts the vehicle's departure from the recommended route at the AYE / West Coast Highway exit at 18:05:06 — three minutes after the acknowledgment. POL-RD-21 provides that where the chat log confirms the rider's acknowledgment the deviation is agreed, and here the chat log does exactly that, on complete artifacts carrying weight 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05006", "EV-TRIP-05006"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's acknowledgment is unrebutted: her counterparty statement objects only that 'the longer road cost more' and never denies that she answered 'ok' to the West Coast Highway proposal, so on POL-RD-21 the deviation was an agreed route choice, not a unilateral detour visited on her. On the platform's recorded distances the deviation is 1.90 km (14.6 minus 12.7, per POL-RD-22's recorded-distance measure), over the 1 km tolerance, which puts the case in POL-RD-24(a) — informed and agreed, over 1 km — rather than the 'not informed' row (b). A row that returns nothing to the rider leaves the 1.37 SGD already recovered from the driver's earnings to be restored to him as DRIVER_COMPENSATION under POL-GEN-03.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05006", "EV-TRIP-05006", "EV-FARE-05006"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-RD-22", "POL-RD-24", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The remedy the driver asks for is the exact figure the platform has already moved: fare_breakdown.refund_issued_sgd 1.37 with payment_status PARTIALLY_REFUNDED, refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver's earnings by the fare_adjusted event at 2026-08-19T01:56:34+08:00. The contested amount is 1.37 SGD — below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so no confidence floor and no value-based escalation applies — and the deviation of 1.90 km is inside POL-RD-25's 2 km limb, so the AI may rule this case on its merits now rather than defer it, and the DRIVER_COMPENSATION figure under POL-GEN-03 is 1.37 SGD.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05006", "EV-TRIP-05006"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-GEN-22", "POL-RD-25"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.refund_already_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "In the alternative, if the traffic limb of POL-RD-23 is not accepted on this record, the case should go to a human rather than be closed against the driver. The AYE advisory (EV-ADVIS-05006-01) returns type NONE, so it records neither incident nor closure and its type is not one of the kinds POL-RD-23 names, while the trip-window closure-kind advisory (EV-ADVIS-05006-02), a ROADWORK valid 09:00–23:00 on 18/8, has an intersection with the route that the same derived block expressly leaves undetermined; against the driver's contemporaneous in-app report of the jam, that limb is not cleanly negated, and where a fact POL-RD-23 needs cannot be established the case is escalated under POL-GEN-26 with the 1.37 SGD held rather than confirmed against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05006-01", "EV-ADVIS-05006-02", "EV-CHAT-05006"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-05006-02.payload.derived.v7.undetermined",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you agree on the essentials, so I can rule this on the record. On the route, the platform's recorded distances put the recommended route at 12.7 km and the route actually driven at 14.6 km (EV-TRIP-05006) — a deviation of 1.90 km, over POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance and inside POL-RD-25's 2 km AI limit. The driver did tell the rider before deviating: MSG-05006-003 at 18:01:46 asked to take West Coast Highway, the rider answered 'ok' at 18:02:11, and the vehicle left the recommended route at 18:05:06 (EV-CHAT-05006, EV-TRIP-05006). So notice and agreement under POL-RD-21 is established, as the driver argues.\n\nAgreement, however, does not answer the traffic question, and POL-RD-24 row (a) needs the reroute to be traffic-justified. POL-RD-23 asks for traffic data on the RECOMMENDED route. The LTA record for the recommended carriageway — Ayer Rajah Expressway towards City, Clementi Road to Keppel Viaduct — covers the whole trip window and is type NONE: no incident, roadwork or closure, speed bands 4-6 (EV-ADVIS-05006-01). The only roadwork in the record (EV-ADVIS-05006-02, Pasir Panjang Road near Pasir Panjang Wholesale Centre) sits on a road the deviating route used, not on the recommended route, so it cannot justify leaving the AYE. The driver's report of a jam is therefore not borne out by the traffic data, and the rider's statement that the AYE looked clear is consistent with it. The driver's alternative request to escalate on this limb is declined: the limb is decided by the advisory on the recommended route, not left undetermined, so POL-GEN-26 is not engaged.\n\nThat puts this in POL-RD-24 row (d): not traffic-justified, deviation over 1 km — the excess distance fare is refunded in full. The excess distance fare is 1.90 km x 0.72 SGD/km = 1.368, rounded half-up to 1.37 SGD (EV-FARE-05006), which is exactly what the platform already moved: 1.37 SGD refunded to the rider and recovered from the driver on 2026-08-19T01:56:34+08:00. The rider is already where the policy puts her.\n\nBecause the driver filed, POL-GEN-03 asks whether the filing party's claim is supported. It is not, so the present state stands and no money moves: NO_ACTION, with no amount in either direction. I do not escalate — the contested value is 1.37 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD line, the deviation is within POL-RD-25's 2 km limb, and neither profile carries a fraud flag — so the AI decides. Confidence is 0.90, above POL-RD-25's 0.80 bar; every artifact this ruling rests on is COMPLETE at a weight_multiplier of 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "This is a route-deviation dispute filed by the driver, D-14860, against the 1.37 SGD the platform refunded to rider R-27563 and recovered from the driver's earnings (fare_adjusted at 2026-08-19T01:56:34+08:00). I have decided it under POL-RD-24's refund matrix and POL-RD-23's traffic-justification rule, and the outcome for the filing party is NO_ACTION: the driver's claim is not supported and the present state stands, so both money fields are null and the 1.37 SGD already refunded stays with the rider.\n\nThe deviation itself is established and over tolerance. On the platform's recorded distances (POL-RD-22 requires the recorded distances, not the sparse trace), the actual route was 14.6 km against an optimal 12.7 km, a deviation of 1.90 km, 0.90 km beyond the 1.0 km tolerance. That is over 1 km and inside POL-RD-25's 2.0 km limit, so the AI may rule.\n\nThe traffic limb fails, and this is what decides the case. POL-RD-23 justifies a reroute only where traffic data for the recommended route segment at the trip time shows congestion, an incident or a closure. EV-ADVIS-05006-01 covers the recommended carriageway, the Ayer Rajah Expressway (AYE) towards City between Clementi Road and Keppel Viaduct, across a window (17:29:34-18:59:34) that brackets the whole trip; its type is NONE, it records no incident, roadwork or closure, and NONE is not one of the kinds POL-RD-23 names. The one non-NONE advisory, EV-ADVIS-05006-02, is a ROADWORK on Pasir Panjang Road towards Telok Blangah. Pasir Panjang Road is not on the recommended route (Clementi Avenue 2, AYE, Keppel Road, Wallich Street); it is a road the deviating route used, so it does not intersect the recommended route and does not supply the justification. The driver's in-app assertion of an 'AYE jam' (MSG-05006-003) is therefore contradicted by the traffic data for the very segment concerned, and the rider's statement that the AYE looked clear as they passed the slip road is consistent with that data. The reroute was not traffic-justified, so POL-RD-24(d) applies: refund of the excess distance fare in full, being 1.90 km x 0.72 SGD per km = 1.368, rounded half-up to 1.37 SGD, exactly the figure in refund_issued_sgd and the figure already moved. The rider is already in the position the policy prescribes; the driver's claim asks to restore a charge the policy says must not stand.\n\nOn the driver's case: notice and agreement are accepted on the record. The driver's message at 18:01:46 and the rider's 'ok' at 18:02:11, read before the 18:05:06 departure at the AYE / West Coast Highway exit, show the rider was informed and agreed, as POL-RD-21 provides. But POL-RD-24(a) — informed, agreed and over 1 km — still requires the reroute to be traffic-justified, and it is not. Agreement to a detour does not convert a non-justified detour into a no-refund case, so the DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 1.37 SGD the driver seeks is refused. The driver's alternative request to escalate under POL-GEN-26 is also refused: the traffic limb is not unestablishable. The two advisories are complete and carry weight 1.0, and between them they show the recommended segment clear and the only closure-kind advisory on a road that is not the recommended route — the limb is decided against the driver, not left open. No fact this case needs is missing, so escalation would hold a sum the arithmetic already settles.\n\nConfidence is 0.85. The deciding facts (the recorded distances and the traffic advisories) are carried by artifacts all at weight_multiplier 1.0, so POL-GEN-02(2)'s cap is 1.0; POL-RD-25 sets the bar at 0.80 for a route deviation and POL-GEN-22 places a 1.37 SGD dispute in the AI-final band with no fraud flag, so the ruling may issue finally. No referral arises: the referral clauses in this version (POL-NS-24, POL-NS-25, POL-NS-22) are no-show clauses and none applies to a route deviation."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
